## Summary

Add a `docket sync` command to push/pull the state branch to/from remote.

## Implementation

New file `src/commands/sync_state.rs` (rename existing sync.rs if needed):

```rust
/// Sync docket state with remote
pub fn sync_state() -> Result<()> {
    // Fetch latest from remote
    println!("{} Fetching state from remote...", "→".blue());
    Command::new("jj")
        .args(["git", "fetch"])
        .status()?;

    // Push local state
    println!("{} Pushing state to remote...", "→".blue());
    Command::new("jj")
        .args(["git", "push", "--bookmark", "docket-state"])
        .status()?;

    println!("{} State synchronized", "✓".green());
    Ok(())
}
```

Add subcommand in main.rs:
```rust
#[derive(Subcommand)]
enum Commands {
    // ...
    /// Sync docket state with remote
    SyncState,
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] docket sync-state command added
- [ ] Fetches remote changes
- [ ] Pushes local state branch
- [ ] Clear status messages
- [ ] Handles no-remote gracefully
